 "answer": "Use the built-in PostgreSQL function **`pg_relation_size()`**. pgvector doesn't add its own size function, so this works for HNSW and IVFFlat indexes like any other index:\n\n```sql\nSELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('my_vector_index'));\n```\n\nRelated functions:\n\n- **`pg_indexes_size('my_table')`** returns the combined size of all indexes on a table.\n- **`pg_total_relation_size('my_table')`** returns the table, its indexes, and TOAST data together.",
